  "gloss": "also, too",
  "title": "juga — also, too",
  "pattern": "Saya juga … · … juga · … juga tidak",
  "explanation": "juga means also or too, and it comes straight after the word it adds to: Saya juga. — Me too. Minta air putih juga. — Some water too, please. Think of it as following whatever is 'as well', so Juga saya, the English order of also me, is wrong. For not … either, juga goes before tidak: Saya juga tidak tahu (I don't know either), or shortened, …, dia juga tidak. In casual speech that's Aku juga nggak.",
  "natural": "Agreeing (Saya juga!), adding something to an order, and saying not either with tidak. Fine in any register.",
  "stiff": "Don't start a sentence with Juga to add a new point (Also, …): that's Selain itu (besides that). And there's no separate word for either: juga with tidak covers it.",
